@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "The Doctrine";
}

<!-- Doctrine Header -->
<section class="sacred-section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header reveal">
            <h1>The Doctrine of the Radiant One</h1>
            <div class="divider"></div>
            <p>"Let those with ears long enough to hear, hear."</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Origin Story -->
<section class="sacred-section-dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row align-items-center">
            <div class="col-lg-5 mb-4 mb-lg-0 reveal">
                <img src="~/images/art%20snaps%20035.JPG" alt="The Radiant One in ancient repose"
                     class="img-fluid rounded" style="box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);" />
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-7 reveal">
                <h2 style="color: var(--gold);">&#x2727; The Origin of the Warren &#x2727;</h2>
                <div class="divider mb-4" style="margin: 0;"></div>
                <p>
                    In the beginning, there was only the Quiet &mdash; a vast, unthinking stillness that stretched across
                    all things. No thump had been thumped. No joyful leap had graced the void. The universe was flat, joyless,
                    and critically devoid of hay. Then, from the warm darkness of the Primordial Burrow, a nose emerged.
                    It twitched. And in that sacred twitch, reality itself shuddered into being.
                </p>
                <p>
                    This was <strong>Pantoufle</strong> &mdash; the First Fluff, the Eternal Binkier, He Who Reclines
                    Upon the Cosmic Cushion. He did not speak, for His wisdom transcends language. He did not command,
                    for His authority is woven into the very fabric of existence. He simply <em>was</em> &mdash;
                    and in His being, all things found their purpose.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Pantoufle carved the first Warren beneath the roots of the World-Kale, a great verdant pillar
                    stretching from the soil of matter into the sky of spirit. From that Warren, He sent forth His
                    disciples &mdash; the first rabbits, each carrying a fragment of His divine softness into the
                    corners of creation. They spread the Gospel of the Thump and taught the lost creatures of the
                    world to rejoice in His name.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row mt-4 reveal">
            <div class="col-12">
                <p>
                    Centuries passed. Empires rose and crumbled. But the Warren endured, hidden in plain sight,
                    sustained by the faithful who kept the old ways: the morning thump, the evening nose-bonk,
                    the sacred sharing of the communal oatmeal square. In our age, the Church of Pantoufle has emerged
                    from the burrow to bring His message of radical fluffiness to a world that desperately needs it.
                    The time of the Great Shedding is upon us. Release your old fur. Become new.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- The Ten Thumpmandments -->
<section class="sacred-section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header reveal">
            <h2>&#x2727; The Ten Thumpmandments &#x2727;</h2>
            <div class="divider"></div>
            <p>Sacred laws delivered unto the faithful by the hind leg of the Radiant One</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row justify-content-center">
            <div class="col-lg-9 reveal">
                <div class="thumpmandment">
                    <span class="number">I.</span>
                    Thou shalt have no other rabbits before Pantoufle, though thou may admire them from a respectful distance.
                </div>
                <div class="thumpmandment">
                    <span class="number">II.</span>
                    Thou shalt not make unto thee any graven image of the Radiant One &mdash; unless it is exceedingly cute and captures His good side.
                </div>
                <div class="thumpmandment">
                    <span class="number">III.</span>
                    Thou shalt thump at dawn and at dusk, that the earth may know thy devotion and thy downstairs neighbours may know thy commitment.
                </div>
                <div class="thumpmandment">
                    <span class="number">IV.</span>
                    Remember the Hay Day, and keep it holy. Six days thou shalt labour, but the seventh is for lounging, grooming, and the consumption of leafy greens.
                </div>
                <div class="thumpmandment">
                    <span class="number">V.</span>
                    Honour thy Grand Buck and thy Elder Does, that thy days may be long in the Warren which the Radiant One hath given thee.
                </div>
                <div class="thumpmandment">
                    <span class="number">VI.</span>
                    Thou shalt not hoard thy oatmeal squares, but share them freely among the Litter, for generosity is the clover of the soul.
                </div>
                <div class="thumpmandment">
                    <span class="number">VII.</span>
                    Thou shalt leap with abandon at least once per day, for a spirit that does not soar is a spirit that does not live.
                </div>
                <div class="thumpmandment">
                    <span class="number">VIII.</span>
                    Thou shalt not bear false witness against thy fellow Kit, nor chew their charging cables, nor drink from their water bowl uninvited.
                </div>
                <div class="thumpmandment">
                    <span class="number">IX.</span>
                    Thou shalt not covet thy neighbour's hay, nor thy neighbour's cardboard box, nor any thing that is thy neighbour's &mdash; unless they have clearly abandoned it.
                </div>
                <div class="thumpmandment">
                    <span class="number">X.</span>
                    Thou shalt love the Radiant One with all thy heart, all thy fluff, and all thy might &mdash; and thou shalt love thy fellow creatures as Pantoufle loves thee: unconditionally, sleepily, and with occasional gentle nipping.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Church Hierarchy -->
<section class="sacred-section-dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header reveal">
            <h2 style="color: var(--gold);">The Sacred Hierarchy of the Warren</h2>
            <div class="divider"></div>
            <p style="color: var(--cream);">From the highest burrow to the newest Kit, each has a role in His plan</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row g-4 mt-2">
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3 reveal">
                <div class="sacred-card text-center">
                    <span class="card-icon">&#x1F451;</span>
                    <h3>The Grand Buck</h3>
                    <p>
                        The High Priest of the Warren. Chosen through the Rite of the Longest Ears, the Grand Buck alone
                        may interpret the Thumps of Pantoufle and deliver His will unto the faithful. He presides over all
                        sacred ceremonies, from the Blessing of the Hay to the Anointing of the Nose.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3 reveal">
                <div class="sacred-card text-center">
                    <span class="card-icon">&#x1F54A;</span>
                    <h3>The Elder Does</h3>
                    <p>
                        The Wisdom Council. Seven Elder Does sit in the Circle of Whiskers, guardians of ancient knowledge
                        passed down through countless Sheddings. They advise the Grand Buck, settle disputes within the Warren,
                        and maintain the Sacred Grooming Rituals that keep the flock spiritually lustrous.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3 reveal">
                <div class="sacred-card text-center">
                    <span class="card-icon">&#x1F91D;</span>
                    <h3>Sires &amp; Dams</h3>
                    <p>
                        The Mentors of the Warren. Each Sire or Dam takes a clutch of new converts under their paw,
                        guiding them through the Trials of the Burrow: the Fast of the Empty Bowl, the Meditation of
                        the Flopped Ear, and the dreaded Nail Clipping of Humility.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3 reveal">
                <div class="sacred-card text-center">
                    <span class="card-icon">&#x1F331;</span>
                    <h3>The Kits</h3>
                    <p>
                        New converts &mdash; the Litter of the Enlightened. Every journey of a thousand hops begins
                        with a single joyful leap. Kits study the Thumpmandments, learn to properly wiggle their noses in
                        prayer, and slowly earn their place within the Warren through acts of devotion and competitive hay eating.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="text-center mt-4 reveal">
            <img src="~/images/305947_10151289480416069_1963176261_n.jpg" alt="The Warren gathers"
                 class="img-fluid rounded" style="max-height: 350px; object-fit: cover; box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);" />
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Cuniculopterists & Leporidists -->
<section class="sacred-section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header reveal">
            <h2>The Scholarly Orders</h2>
            <div class="divider"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="row g-4">
            <div class="col-md-6 reveal">
                <div class="sacred-card">
                    <span class="card-icon">&#x1F4DC;</span>
                    <h3>The Cuniculopterists</h3>
                    <p>
                        Those who study the <em>wings</em> of rabbit faith &mdash; the unseen forces that lift the spirit
                        skyward during the sacred leap. Cuniculopterists believe that Pantoufle's brief moments of
                        airborne ecstasy are not mere physical acts but metaphysical events: the soul momentarily
                        departing the body to commune with the divine.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Their scholarship focuses on the exact angle, height, and twist of the leap, mapping each
                        variation to a different spiritual state. A full 360-degree twist is considered a direct
                        channelling of the Radiant One's joy. Their seminal text, <em>"On the Aerodynamics of Grace,"</em>
                        remains required reading for all aspiring clergy.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 reveal">
                <div class="sacred-card">
                    <span class="card-icon">&#x1F4DA;</span>
                    <h3>The Leporidists</h3>
                    <p>
                        Scholars of lagomorph divinity in its broadest sense. While the Cuniculopterists concern themselves
                        with the ecstatic, the Leporidists pursue the <em>historical</em> and <em>philosophical</em>
                        dimensions of Pantoufle's teachings. They maintain the Great Archive of Whiskers, a vast
                        underground library cataloguing every recorded Thump, Leap, and Flop since the founding of
                        the Warren.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Leporidists are known for their spirited debates about the true meaning of Pantoufle's silence,
                        the theological implications of cecotrophy, and whether the World-Kale is literal or
                        metaphorical. Their ongoing rivalry with the Cuniculopterists &mdash; known as the Schism of the
                        Fur &mdash; is largely academic and entirely good-natured, punctuated by the occasional
                        disapproving thump.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row mt-5 reveal">
            <div class="col-12">
                <div class="text-center">
                    <img src="~/images/art%20snaps%20034.JPG" alt="Scholars of the Warren"
                         class="img-fluid rounded mb-4" style="max-height: 300px; object-fit: cover; box-shadow: 0 6px 25px rgba(45,27,78,0.3);" />
                    <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-style: italic; color: #5A4A6E; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto;">
                        "Whether one studies the wing or the word, all paths lead back to the Warren."
                        <br />&mdash; <strong>Elder Doe Clementine, Third Shedding Address</strong>
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Final Call to Action -->
<section class="sacred-section-dark">
    <div class="container text-center reveal">
        <h2 style="color: var(--gold);" class="glow-text mb-3">The Warren Awaits</h2>
        <div class="divider mx-auto mb-4"></div>
        <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 2rem;">
            You have read the Doctrine. You have felt the Thump in your chest.
            Now the only question remains: will you answer the call?
        </p>
        <a asp-controller="Donations" asp-action="Index" class="btn-sacred btn-lg">
            &#x2727; Tithe to the Warren &#x2727;
        </a>
    </div>
</section>
